.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt TRACE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm trace
.Nd print the recorded span sink as a request tree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
maps the shared span sink at the fixed address
.Pa 0x3000_0000
and drains every committed record from the
.Pa raven-trace-core
ring.
It prints a summary line followed by one line per span:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
trace: spans=<n> gaps=<n> traced=<n> untraced=<n>
trace: id=<id> span=<span> parent=<parent> pid=<pid> ts=<ns> kind=<kind> op=<op>
.Ed
.Pp
The summary counts spans whose trace id is zero as
.Ql untraced .
A span line prints a zero trace id as
.Ql untraced
and a non-zero id as
.Ql 0x
followed by the lower-case hexadecimal value.
The
.Ql kind
field is one of
.Ql client ,
.Ql server ,
.Ql kernel
or
.Ql io ;
.Ql op
is the wire opcode of the recorded request.
.Pp
The sink is created and populated by the process that spawned
.Nm ,
which transfers the sink memory object before the first thread starts.
The current implementation is the Q4b fixture harness:
.Pa tests/fixtures/trace-demo
creates the sink, runs a scheme server that records spans with the caller's inherited trace id, and
then runs
.Nm
to print the result.
A real
.Xr vfsd 8
tree follows in Q4.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
An unreadable or malformed sink exits with status 1.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfsd 8
